.TH "mpvc-chapter" "1" "April, 2026" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
mpvc-chapter - manage and merge ffmetadata chapter files for mpvc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
usage: mpvc-chapter args # \[at]version v1.9 (c) gmt4 https://github.com/gmt4/mpvc
 (--)list : List ffmetadata chapter-files
 (--)file : Show current ffmetadata chapter-file
 (--)info : Info current ffmetadata chapter-file
 (--)reset: Reset current ffmetadata chapter-file
 (--)load : Load current ffmetadata chapter-file
 (--)gen  : Gen a ffmetadata chapter-file from a < chapterlist.txt
 (--)merge: Merge ffmetadata chapter-file to audio file (args: in ffmeta out)
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
mpvc-chapter is a utility helper script bundled with mpvc that automates
the tracking, creation, parsing, and merging of chapter structures
within media files using FFmpeg\[cq]s ffmetadata format container layout
maps.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--list\f[B]\f[R]
List all compiled or cached ffmetadata chapter files currently tracking
active streaming or media profiles.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--file\f[B]\f[R]
Print the absolute path of the currently active ffmetadata chapter asset
configuration.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--info\f[B]\f[R]
Display metadata headers, timestamp tracks, layout intervals, and
internal structure properties contained within the active chapter file.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--reset\f[B]\f[R]
Wipe, clear, and re-initialize the target chapter configuration metadata
layout map back to pristine system defaults.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--load\f[B]\f[R]
Explicitly register and hot-load the active chapter markers map directly
into the running instance workspace.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--gen\f[B]\f[R]
Generate a syntactically correct ffmetadata map stream file parsed from
standard input.
This reads sequential text layouts containing raw timestamp intervals
and titles.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--merge\f[B]\f[R]
Merge a standalone ffmetadata layout directly back into a targeted
physical media container.
This command strictly requires three continuous sequential file
parameters passed as trailing arguments: the input audio file, the
source ffmetadata map file, and the output destination container path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Generate an ffmetadata chapter map file from a text listing input stream
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
    mpvc-chapter --gen < chapterlist.txt
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Bake an extracted or parsed metadata layout map directly into an audio
track file
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
    mpvc-chapter --merge input.mp3 track_layout.ffmeta processed_album.mp3
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
List all tracked workspace chapter files
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
    mpvc-chapter --list
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Check properties and internal metadata of the active tracking file
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
    mpvc-chapter --info
\f[R]
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
MPV_SOCKET
Override the default MPV socket path.
Used by internal companion script wrappers to identify which instance
target context boundaries apply.
.TP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Directory where mpvc configurations are systematically discovered.
Defaults to \[ti]/.config/ if not specified by your shell environment
variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
\[ti]/.config/mpvc/mpvc.conf
Core mpvc-specific runtime configurations, variable flags, and system
mapping settings.
